    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RE/MAX Property Specialists are delighted to present Crinalisk, Kill, Co. Waterford to the market, a distinctive and beautifully presented four-bedroom, two-bathroom detached timber residence, set on a generous site of approximately 0.75 acres.\r\n\r\nThe property immediately stands out for its striking Scandinavian-inspired design, warm timber construction and impressive setting. Surrounded by sweeping lawns, mature hedging and established planting, Crinalisk offers an excellent sense of space and privacy, while a substantial tarmac driveway surrounds the residence and provides ample parking for numerous vehicles.\r\n\r\nInternally, the home is filled with character, with extensive natural timber walls, ceilings and flooring creating a warm and inviting atmosphere throughout.\r\nA bright entrance porch leads into the impressive main living room, a particularly generous reception space. Large windows allow excellent natural light into the room and provide views across the surrounding gardens, while a feature fireplace creates an attractive focal point. An open timber staircase rises through the living space to the upper floor and further enhances the character of the home.\r\n\r\nThe spacious kitchen is fitted with contemporary cabinetry, generous worktop space and integrated appliances. Tiled flooring provides a practical finish, while direct access to the exterior makes the kitchen particularly convenient for everyday family living and outdoor entertaining. Two generously proportioned bedrooms are positioned on the ground floor, providing excellent flexibility for family accommodation, guests or a home office. A well-appointed family bathroom, complete with shower, completes the ground-floor accommodation.\r\n\r\nThe upper floor continues the property's distinctive timber finish and provides an exceptionally spacious principal bedroom with high ceilings, extensive natural light and ample space for bedroom furniture. The bedroom also benefits from a substantial dressing and wardrobe area, providing excellent storage. A second bathroom serves this level.\r\n\r\nOne of the particularly appealing features of the upper floor is the covered balcony, which provides an attractive sheltered outdoor space overlooking the grounds and surrounding countryside.\r\n\r\nOutside, Crinalisk is complemented by particularly impressive gardens. Expansive lawns extend around the residence and are bordered by mature hedging, trees and established planting, creating an attractive and private setting with considerable space for recreation and outdoor living. The property also benefits from a timber garden shed and extensive hardstanding around the house.\r\n\r\nThe property enjoys a peaceful countryside setting close to Kill village and is well positioned for exploring the wider Waterford coastline. The renowned Copper Coast UNESCO Global Geopark is within easy reach, offering dramatic coastal scenery, walking routes, hidden coves and beaches. Nearby Bunmahon Beach is popular for surfing, kayaking and coastal activities, while Kilmurrin Beach provides another attractive option for swimming, walking and enjoying the coastline.\r\n\r\nFurther features include oil-fired central heating, double-glazed windows, fibre broadband, a private well and septic tank. The property has a B BER rating.\r\nCombining distinctive architecture, spacious four-bedroom accommodation, exceptionally generous gardens and easy access to the Copper Coast, Crinalisk offers a unique countryside home within easy reach of Kill and the wider Co. Waterford area.\r\n\r\nThese particulars do not constitute an offer or contract, and whilst every effort has been made in preparing all descriptions, dimensions, maps, and plans, these details should not be relied upon as fact. Dimensions / Illustrations are for guideline purposes only and not to scale. RE/MAX Property Specialists - Team fogarty will not hold itself responsible for any inaccuracies contained therein"
      },
